#EXTM3U
# StreamForge Hub — Tivify live channels (LAN gateway 192.168.129.5:8890)
#
# Why the addresses look like this:
#   * 192.168.129.5 is the Fire TV's LAN address. 127.0.0.1 only works on the
#     device itself, so a TiviMate box or IPTVnator on a PC could never tune it.
#   * the .m3u8 suffix is required by strict players (IPTVnator's Chromium
#     player factory refuses an extension-less URL).
#   * EXTVLCOPT / KODIPROP repeat the TVUp player identity for clients that
#     fetch the stream themselves; the gateway also injects it server-side.
#   * tivify://channel/<code> is the same channel as an internal reference and
#     is what the hub resolves without any loopback HTTP call.

#EXTINF:-1 tvg-id="INF70" tvg-name="France 24 English" tvg-logo="" group-title="Tivify",France 24 English
#EXTVLCOPT:http-user-agent=Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/122.0.0.0 Safari/537.36
#EXTVLCOPT:http-referrer=https://tivify.es/
#KODIPROP:inputstream.adaptive.stream_headers=User-Agent=Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/122.0.0.0 Safari/537.36&Referer=https://tivify.es/
http://192.168.129.5:8890/plugins/tivify/INF70.m3u8

#EXTINF:-1 tvg-id="INF60" tvg-name="France 24 Español" tvg-logo="" group-title="Tivify",France 24 Español
#EXTVLCOPT:http-user-agent=Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/122.0.0.0 Safari/537.36
#EXTVLCOPT:http-referrer=https://tivify.es/
#KODIPROP:inputstream.adaptive.stream_headers=User-Agent=Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/122.0.0.0 Safari/537.36&Referer=https://tivify.es/
http://192.168.129.5:8890/plugins/tivify/INF60.m3u8

